Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:05:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 93/94] doc: the rescue lane's accepted risks, wallet duties
 and provenance after review

Two reviews of the final proof system by AI models found no forgery, no
malleability and no way around the rules, and asked for documentation:
doc/p2mr-rescue.md now records the accepted risks (NIST category 1 against
known quantum attacks, security in the quantum random oracle model only
conjectured, a seed of at least 128 bits, no external review), what
wallets and operators must do that the node cannot check, why network_id
is untagged, what limits an input to one rescue check, the weight's
measurements at 130,000 on two machines, and where a cross build's
functional tests take their prover.

src/rescue/README.md names the republished ark0-rescue commit 3c90cd4,
the same tree as f5a2bc0, and SPEC.md v0.2 revision 3 (wording only);
the test tools are built only natively. When no prover is found, the test
framework's message also names VOLEITH_PROVE.
