+**Accepted risks.** For a test network, this build accepts as a recorded decision:
+
+- strength at NIST category 1 against known quantum attacks: about `2^64` Grover iterations, for `Δ`
+  or for a hidden seed of a proof (`SPEC.md` sections 13.5 and 13.6);
+- security in the quantum random oracle model as a conjecture only;
+- that a wallet's seed has at least 128 bits of entropy (`SPEC.md` section 13.1): a weaker seed makes
+  the lane weaker than the proof system;
+- no external review of the proof system or of its implementations.
+
+A larger margin needs a larger security parameter, which the proof size does not allow.
+
