 ## Activation
 
@@ -205,6 +224,30 @@ marked invalid: `bitcoin-cli reconsiderblock <hash of that block>` lets it conti
 "A transaction with a rescue record" is one structural test, shared by items 2, 4 and 5: an input
 whose witness has at least two elements, the last of which starts with `0x50 0x01`. It reads no coin.
 
+## Wallets and operators
+
+The node cannot check what follows; ark0-rescue `SPEC.md` section 12.1 item 4 requires it of every
+rescue.
+
+- Rescue all frozen outputs of a key together, in one transaction, so that none of them waits on the
+  freeze alone once `d` is public. A standard transaction holds at most three rescue inputs
+  ([Policy](#policy), item 3); a key with more frozen outputs needs one transaction that the block
+  producer includes directly, and a block holds about 30 rescue inputs.
+- Before the first rescue, move by an ordinary spend every output that the same key `P` can spend
+  another way: a leaf of version `0xc0`, a P2TR output with the same key, a legacy or witness v0
+  script, or an output on another network. The freeze covers an output only where `P` is checked in
+  a leaf of version `0xe0`, regardless of when the output was created.
+- Never reuse the key, `d` or the seed on another network or protocol, and pay nothing more to `P`
+  once it is burned.
+- Make a rescue only once the block that triggered the freeze has enough confirmations (the mempool
+  refuses it before the checks are disabled, [Policy](#policy) item 2), and do not extend a branch
+  that undoes that block: after such a reorganization `d` is public while the checks work again. A
+  block producer that includes a rescue transaction directly, outside the mempool, must check that
+  the checks are disabled itself.
+- Proofs are made off the node, with the prover of ark0-rescue. Its Rust prover is written to be
+  constant time and to clear its secrets, but no external review has checked that; use it only with
+  seeds used on this signet alone.
+
